"ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F8.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F8.pic1.1" class="ltx_text"> (Mi)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -32.5 51.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="24.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F8.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">FID</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000"><path d="M 3.99 3.38 h 54.1 v 26.44 h -54.1 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.14 9.56)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 20.91)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 3.6)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.55,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 7.48 0 L 14.96 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 16.07 0) translate(14.87,0) matrix(0.4 0.0 0.0 0.4 -13.76 -1.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:4.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="67.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">EDM (self)</span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 10.64)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.55,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 7.48 0 L 14.96 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 23.95 0) translate(6.99,0) matrix(0.4 0.0 0.0 0.4 -5.88 -1.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:2.15em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="29.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Flow</span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.49)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.55,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 7.48 0 L 14.96 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 23.75 0) translate(7.18,0) matrix(0.4 0.0 0.0 0.4 -6.07 -1.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:2.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="30.36"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">IMM</span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><span id="S4.F8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Neon supports cross-architecture synthetic data transfer.</span>
We illustrate by using synthetic data from an IMM and a Flow model to improve EDM-VP on CIFAR-10. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Data from a flow matching model achieves an FID of 1.59, and from an IMM model reaches 1.80. The theory expounded in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS6" title="B.6 Neighbor models: stability and uniform Neon improvement ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> formalizes why Neon is transferable.
Consider models
<math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimize the same objective with Hessians <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If these Hessians are spectrally close (equivalent norms up to constants <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C</annotation></semantics></math>) and the architectures induce similar sampler biases (small mismatch <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> in the terms <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> defined in
(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.1 Why Neon Works ‣ 3 Neon: Negative Extrapolation from Self-Training ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), then anti-alignment transfers from one model to the other.
That is, when model <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(\mathsf{A})}\leq-\mu&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(\mathsf{A})}\leq-\mu&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, any nearby model <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{B})</annotation></semantics></math> inherits <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s^{(\mathsf{B})}\leq-\mu/2&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(\mathsf{B})}\leq-\mu/2&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Intuitively, models learning similar representations exhibit similar overconfidence patterns, and so one model’s degradation direction corrects another’s biases.
This makes Neon practical when generating samples from the target model is costly.</p>
</div>
