</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize our results and provide a comprehensive comparison with state-of-the-art generative models in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table A.1 ‣ Appendix A State of the art comparison ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. The following section discusses Neon’s performance on each benchmark in more detail, highlighting its standing relative to top-performing models and other post-hoc methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CIFAR-10</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On both conditional and unconditional CIFAR-10, Neon improves the EDM-VP baseline to a <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.38 FID</span> while maintaining its 35 NFE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. In the conditional setting, this is competitive with DDO, which achieves a 1.30 FID from the same base model but requires significantly more training compute ( 12% extra vs. Neon’s 1.75%) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. In the unconditional setting, Neon’s 1.38 FID is identical to DDO’s and close to the SOTA held by SIMS at 1.33 FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alemohammad et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. Notably, SIMS requires doubling the NFE to 70, making Neon a more sampling-efficient alternative. Neon also demonstrates versatility by improving a Flow Matching model to a 2.32 FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">FFHQ-64x64</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On FFHQ, Neon significantly enhances the unconditional EDM-VP model, lowering its FID from 2.39 to <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.12</span> with 79 NFE. While the state-of-the-art is held by the one-step D2O-F at 0.85 FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng &amp; Yang, 2025</a>)</cite>, Neon’s performance is highly competitive. It stands against other post-hoc methods like SIMS (1.04 FID, 158 NFE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alemohammad et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> and the one-step distilled SiD<sup id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>A (1.04 FID, 1 NFE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. Neon achieves its strong result with a simple parameter merge that preserves the base sampler’s structure, offering a distinct trade-off between FID and NFE.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ImageNet-256x256</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On ImageNet-256, Neon sets a new <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">state-of-the-art</span>, improving the xAR-L model from an already strong 1.28 FID to <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.02 FID</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. This surpasses the previous best result of 1.06 FID from REPA-UCGM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Neon also demonstrates its superiority over DDO on this benchmark; when applied to the same VAR-d16 base model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Neon achieves a 2.01 FID, which is a significant improvement over DDO’s 2.54 FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Furthermore, Neon consistently improves other architectures, including xAR-B (1.31 FID) and IMM (1.46 FID).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ImageNet-512x512</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On ImageNet-512, Neon improves the VAR-d30 model to a <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.70 FID</span> with 10 NFE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. While the state-of-the-art belongs to EDM2-L+DDO at 1.21 FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, Neon’s result is competitive with other post-hoc methods applied to different base models, such as EDM2-S+SIMS (1.73 FID) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alemohammad et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. It showcases Neon’s ability to enhance autoregressive models at higher resolutions with its characteristic low compute overhead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across all benchmarks, Neon proves to be a simple, efficient, and broadly applicable post-hoc method for improving generative models. It achieves a new state-of-the-art on ImageNet-256 and delivers highly competitive results elsewhere, often with superior sampling efficiency compared to other post-hoc techniques. A key finding is that Neon’s effectiveness corresponds directly to the quality of the base model it enhances; applying it to a stronger foundation like xAR-L yields a greater improvement and the best overall performance. This positions Neon as a reliable tool for adding a final layer of polish to strong, pre-existing generative models with minimal computational effort. Crucially, since Neon improves the base diffusion model itself, its benefits are potentially orthogonal to distillation methods; one could apply SiD<sup id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>A or D2O-F to the Neon-enhanced model for further gains.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs and Detailed Explanations</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Assumptions, notation, and identities</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumptions.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be a differentiable per-example loss and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[\ell_{\theta}(X)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[\ell_{\theta}(X)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A1)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data risk minimizer.</span> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\arg\min_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\arg\min_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\theta}(x):=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\theta}(x):=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A2)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regularity.</span> Common support; dominated convergence/interchange of limits and expectations; local Lipschitz of <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\theta}(x):=\partial_{\theta}\phi_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\theta}(x):=\partial_{\theta}\phi_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A3)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local neighborhood.</span> <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with small <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>; all remainders are <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{\,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{\,2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A4)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank.</span> If <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is not full rank, interpret all statements on <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Im}(H_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Im}(H_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metric and basic objects.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data Hessian is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>-induced geometry</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle_{M}:=x^{\top}My,\quad\|x\|_{M}:=\|M^{1/2}x\|_{2},\quad\|A\|_{\mathrm{op},M}:=\|M^{1/2}AM^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>M</mi><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle_{M}:=x^{\top}My,\quad\|x\|_{M}:=\|M^{1/2}x\|_{2},\quad\|A\|_{\mathrm{op},M}:=\|M^{1/2}AM^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and write <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{H_{d}},\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{H_{d}},\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a preconditioner <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> with bounds <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mI\preceq K\preceq MI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mI\preceq K\preceq MI</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Neon improves under anti-alignment</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alignment scalar and synthetic objective.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{d}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}[\ell_{\theta}(X)],\qquad r_{s}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>syn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>syn</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{d}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}[\ell_{\theta}(X)],\qquad r_{s}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define the alignment scalar</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;:=\;\langle r_{d},\;P\,r_{s}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;:=\;\langle r_{d},\;P\,r_{s}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step Neon improvement)<span id="Thmtheorem1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A short synthetic fine-tune produces
<math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha\,Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha\,Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the Neon merge is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{Neon}}\;=\;(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}\;=\;\theta_{r}+w\alpha\,Pr_{s}+O(w\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Neon</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{Neon}}\;=\;(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}\;=\;\theta_{r}+w\alpha\,Pr_{s}+O(w\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{d}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{d}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})\;=\;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;+\;w\alpha\,s\;+\;\frac{(w\alpha)^{2}}{2}\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}\,P\,r_{s}\;+\;O\big((w\alpha)^{3}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Neon</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})\;=\;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;+\;w\alpha\,s\;+\;\frac{(w\alpha)^{2}}{2}\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}\,P\,r_{s}\;+\;O\big((w\alpha)^{3}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> then for all sufficiently small <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we have
<math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})&lt;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Neon</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})&lt;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>.
If moreover <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{d}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{d}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, writing <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
any</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;&lt;\;w\;&lt;\;-\,\frac{2s}{\alpha q}\quad\text{guarantees}\quad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\ \ (\text{up to }O((w\alpha)^{3}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">guarantees</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Neon</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;&lt;\;w\;&lt;\;-\,\frac{2s}{\alpha q}\quad\text{guarantees}\quad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\ \ (\text{up to }O((w\alpha)^{3})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the quadratic proxy is minimized at <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w^{*}=-\,{s}/{(\alpha q)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{*}=-\,{s}/{(\alpha q)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the short synthetic fine-tune we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{Neon}}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}+w\alpha\,Pr_{s}\;+\;O(w\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Neon</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{Neon}}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}+w\alpha\,Pr_{s}\;+\;O(w\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the univariate function</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\tau):=\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\big(\theta_{r}+\tau\,Pr_{s}\big),\qquad\text{and set }\;\tau=w\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and set </mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\tau):=\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\big(\theta_{r}+\tau\,Pr_{s}\big),\qquad\text{and set }\;\tau=w\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">A Taylor expansion of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\tau)=\psi(0)\;+\;\tau\,\psi^{\prime}(0)\;+\;\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)\;+\;O(\tau^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\tau)=\psi(0)\;+\;\tau\,\psi^{\prime}(0)\;+\;\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)\;+\;O(\tau^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}(0)=\big\langle r_{d},\;Pr_{s}\big\rangle\;=\;s,\qquad\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\,\widehat{H}_{d}\,P\,r_{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}(0)=\big\langle r_{d},\;Pr_{s}\big\rangle\;=\;s,\qquad\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\,\widehat{H}_{d}\,P\,r_{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=w\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=w\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})=\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;+\;w\alpha\,s\;+\;\frac{(w\alpha)^{2}}{2}\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}\;+\;O\!\big((w\alpha)^{3}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Neon</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})=\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;+\;w\alpha\,s\;+\;\frac{(w\alpha)^{2}}{2}\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}\;+\;O\!\big((w\alpha)^{3}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is equation <a href="#A2.E2" title="In Theorem B.1 (One-step Neon improvement). ‣ Alignment scalar and synthetic objective. ‣ B.2 Neon improves under anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the linear term is negative and dominates for sufficiently small <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})&lt;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Neon</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{\text{Neon}})&lt;\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">If, in addition, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{d}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{d}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and the quadratic proxy
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\mapsto\psi(0)+\tau s+\tfrac{1}{2}\tau^{2}\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\mapsto\psi(0)+\tau s+\tfrac{1}{2}\tau^{2}\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized at</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{*}\;=\;-\,\frac{s}{\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}\;&gt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{*}\;=\;-\,\frac{s}{\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=w\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=w\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives the safe window
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;w&lt;-\tfrac{2s}{\alpha\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;w&lt;-\tfrac{2s}{\alpha\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>
and the minimizer
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{*}=-\,\dfrac{s}{\alpha\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}\;=\;-\,\dfrac{s}{\alpha\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{*}=-\,\dfrac{s}{\alpha\,\psi^{\prime\prime}(0)}\;=\;-\,\dfrac{s}{\alpha\,r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}Pr_{s}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(No convexity needed: directional smoothness)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The PSD requirement on <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> can be replaced by an upper curvature bound <em id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">along the step direction</em>
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d:=Pr_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d:=Pr_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. If there is <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{dir}}\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{dir}}\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r}+\tau d)d\leq L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r}+\tau d)d\leq L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the same conclusion holds whenever
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;w&lt;-\frac{2s}{\alpha\,L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d\|_{2}^{2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;w&lt;-\frac{2s}{\alpha\,L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d\|_{2}^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>An upper bound on <math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Local expansion at <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order expansions of real and synthetic gradients)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> small and assume </span>(A1)–(A4)<span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{d}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{d}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and, with</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big],\qquad\Delta\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\;-\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big],\qquad\Delta\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\;-\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{s}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;+\;\underbrace{\big(b+\Delta\,\varepsilon\big)}_{=:R_{\kappa}}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>syn</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ε</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}:=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{syn}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;+\;\underbrace{\big(b+\Delta\,\varepsilon\big)}_{=:R_{\kappa}}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-order expansion of the per-example gradient.</span>
By (A2) (regularity) and a first-order Taylor expansion at <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\theta_{r}}(x)\;=\;\phi_{\theta^{*}}(x)\;+\;H_{\theta^{*}}(x)\,\varepsilon\;+\;\rho(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\theta_{r}}(x)\;=\;\phi_{\theta^{*}}(x)\;+\;H_{\theta^{*}}(x)\,\varepsilon\;+\;\rho(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the remainder satisfies
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\|\rho(X)\|\big]=O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\|\rho(X)\|\big]=O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>
and similarly
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\|\rho(X)\|\big]=O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\|\rho(X)\|\big]=O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Real-risk gradient.</span>
Taking expectation under <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> and using (A1)–(A3),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{d}=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta_{r}}(X)\big]=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=\,0}+\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\varepsilon+\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\rho(X)\big]=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{d}=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta_{r}}(X)\big]=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=\,0}+\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\varepsilon+\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}\!\big[\rho(X)\big]=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Synthetic-risk gradient.</span>
Taking expectation under <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{s}=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta_{r}}(X)\big]=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=:~b}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=~H_{d}+\Delta}\varepsilon+\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\rho(X)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.548em">:</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.548em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta_{r}}(X)\big]=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=:~b}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[H_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]}_{=~H_{d}+\Delta}\varepsilon+\mathbb{E}_{q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\rho(X)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}=b+(H_{d}+\Delta)\,\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=b+(H_{d}+\Delta)\,\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equivalent residual form used later.</span>
It is convenient (and used in subsequent bounds) to rewrite this as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;-\;R_{\kappa}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),\qquad\text{where}\quad R_{\kappa}\;:=\;-\,\big(b+\Delta\,\varepsilon\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=H_{d}\,\varepsilon\;-\;R_{\kappa}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),\qquad\text{where}\quad R_{\kappa}\;:=\;-\,\big(b+\Delta\,\varepsilon\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Both expressions are identical up to the first-order terms, and the latter
isolates the “useful” <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> part from the sampler-induced
mismatch <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Angle and magnitudes.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>–whitened magnitudes</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}:=\|b\|_{H_{d}^{-1}},\qquad\eta_{1}:=\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op},\,H_{d}^{-1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}:=\|b\|_{H_{d}^{-1}},\qquad\eta_{1}:=\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op},\,H_{d}^{-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the angle</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\;:=\;\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\;H_{d}^{-1}b\big\rangle_{H_{d}}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big\|H_{d}^{-1}b\big\|_{H_{d}}}\in[-1,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\;:=\;\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\;H_{d}^{-1}b\big\rangle_{H_{d}}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big\|H_{d}^{-1}b\big\|_{H_{d}}}\in[-1,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is the Euclidean angle between <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{d}^{-1/2}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{-1/2}b</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> with spectral bounds <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mI\preceq K\preceq MI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mI\preceq K\preceq MI</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Directional upper bound for <math id="Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> small,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\leq\;M(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[-\,\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\leq\;M(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[-\,\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, a sufficient condition for <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\qquad\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\;&lt;\;\frac{m\,\eta_{0}}{M(1+\eta_{1})}\,\big(-\cos\varphi\big)\quad\text{with }\cos\varphi&lt;0.\qquad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">with </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\qquad\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\;&lt;\;\frac{m\,\eta_{0}}{M(1+\eta_{1})}\,\big(-\cos\varphi\big)\quad\text{with }\cos\varphi&lt;0.\qquad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (First-order expansions of real and synthetic gradients). ‣ Local expansion at 𝜃_𝑟. ‣ B.3 An upper bound on 𝑠 and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, write</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}PH_{d}\varepsilon\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}Pb\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}P\Delta\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}PH_{d}\varepsilon\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}Pb\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}P\Delta\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Whiten with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> to get</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}\,a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}\,a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now bound the three pieces:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}Ka\leq M\|a\|_{2}^{2}=M\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2},\qquad-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\leq M\,\eta_{1}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}Ka\leq M\|a\|_{2}^{2}=M\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2},\qquad-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\leq M\,\eta_{1}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">For the linear term, write <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}K\tilde{b}=\|K^{1/2}a\|_{2}\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|_{2}\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}K\tilde{b}=\|K^{1/2}a\|_{2}\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|_{2}\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> the angle between <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{1/2}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1/2}a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{1/2}\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1/2}\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|K^{1/2}x\|_{2}\geq\sqrt{m}\|x\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|K^{1/2}x\|_{2}\geq\sqrt{m}\|x\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;\geq\;m\,\|a\|_{2}\,\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}\,[\cos\theta]_{+}\;=\;m\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\eta_{0}\,[\cos\varphi]_{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;\geq\;m\,\|a\|_{2}\,\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}\,[\cos\theta]_{+}\;=\;m\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\eta_{0}\,[\cos\varphi]_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\leq-\,m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,[\cos\varphi]_{+}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\leq-\,m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,[\cos\varphi]_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Since <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cos\varphi]_{+}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cos\varphi]_{+}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\,-\cos\varphi\,]_{+}\geq[\cos\varphi]_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\,-\cos\varphi\,]_{+}\geq[\cos\varphi]_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can replace <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-[\cos\varphi]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-[\cos\varphi]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by the slightly looser but sign-robust term
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-[\,-\cos\varphi\,]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-[\,-\cos\varphi\,]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the stated bound after collecting terms and absorbing <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Natural-gradient geometry)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=H_{d}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=H_{d}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=I</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=M=1</annotation></semantics></math>) and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\leq\;(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[-\,\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\leq\;(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[-\,\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus it suffices that
<math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}&lt;\dfrac{\eta_{0}}{1+\eta_{1}}\,\big(-\cos\varphi\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}&lt;\dfrac{\eta_{0}}{1+\eta_{1}}\,\big(-\cos\varphi\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> to guarantee <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the sampler’s <em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linear bias</em> (whitened by <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>); <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> its <em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">curvature tilt</em>.
From Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem B.4 (Directional upper bound for 𝑠). ‣ Angle and magnitudes. ‣ B.3 An upper bound on 𝑠 and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, the leading terms obey</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\lesssim\;M(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,(-\cos\varphi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\lesssim\;M(1+\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;m\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,(-\cos\varphi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so whenever the angle is <em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">obtuse</em> (<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{-1}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{-1}b</annotation></semantics></math> points mostly <em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">against</em> <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>),
the subtractive linear term eventually dominates as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Equivalently: there exists a threshold <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (depending on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,M,\eta_{0},\eta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,M,\eta_{0},\eta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\cos\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\cos\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>) such that
if the model is sufficiently close to optimal,
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}&lt;\varepsilon_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}&lt;\varepsilon_{0},</annotation></semantics></math>
then <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this small-error regime, Neon reduces the real-data risk by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem B.1 (One-step Neon improvement). ‣ Alignment scalar and synthetic objective. ‣ B.2 Neon improves under anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What remains.</span> The next subsections show that under the common inference rules we study,
the angle condition <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds to first order:
for autoregressive models (temperature <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, top-<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, top-<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>), and for diffusion/flow models under finite-step ODE sampling.
We therefore avoid restating separate plug-in corollaries and simply point back to the bound above.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Acute-angle conditions that imply <math id="A2.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (AR models)</h3>

<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Loss and geometry (AR).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For autoregressive (AR) models we use negative log-likelihood:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}(x)=-\log p_{\theta}(x),\qquad\phi_{\theta}(x)=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(x)=-u_{\theta}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}(x)=-\log p_{\theta}(x),\qquad\phi_{\theta}(x)=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(x)=-u_{\theta}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so the data Hessian is the Fisher, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}=F=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[u_{\theta^{*}}u_{\theta^{*}}^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}=F=\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[u_{\theta^{*}}u_{\theta^{*}}^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a sampler <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\;=\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[u_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[\phi_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big]\;=\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[u_{\theta^{*}}(X)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Our global angle is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\;:=\;\frac{\langle\varepsilon,\;F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\,\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\in[-1,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\;:=\;\frac{\langle\varepsilon,\;F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\,\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\in[-1,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so <em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">anti-alignment</em> corresponds to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Definition (mode-seeking samplers).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We call <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mode-seeking</em> if it is a monotone reweighting of the reference model:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x)\ \propto\ w(x)\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x),\qquad w(x)=f\!\big(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.427em;" width="0.427em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x)\ \propto\ w(x)\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x),\qquad w(x)=f\!\big(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> nondecreasing and not a.e. constant.
(For AR decoding applied tokenwise, the overall sequence law inherits a product of such nondecreasing reweights; we write it as <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity.)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Common AR samplers are mode-seeking.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temperature</span> <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. The sampler draws from <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\propto p_{\theta_{r}}^{1/\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\propto p_{\theta_{r}}^{1/\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z)=\exp\{(1/\tau-1)\,z\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=\exp\{(1/\tau-1)\,z\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\tau-1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\tau-1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing (neutral only at <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top-<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span>. Keep only the <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> largest probabilities: there exists a threshold <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(z)=\mathbb{1}\{z\geq z_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=\mathbb{1}\{z\geq z_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, a nondecreasing step function (neutral only at <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=</annotation></semantics></math> vocabulary size).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top-<math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (nucleus)</span>. Keep the smallest set whose cumulative mass exceeds <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>; this induces a (context-dependent) threshold <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(z)=\mathbb{1}\{z\geq z_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=\mathbb{1}\{z\geq z_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, again nondecreasing (neutral only at <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mode-seeking <math id="Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (first order))<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x)\propto f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x)\propto f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> nondecreasing.
For <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\;&lt;\;0\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\;&lt;\;0\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x):=\varepsilon^{\top}u_{\theta^{*}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x):=\varepsilon^{\top}u_{\theta^{*}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}=\varepsilon^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}(X)]=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[B(X)\big]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[\,w\,B\,]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[\,w\,]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}=\varepsilon^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}(X)]=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\big[B(X)\big]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[\,w\,B\,]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[\,w\,]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">A first-order expansion around <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)=\log p_{\theta^{*}}(x)\;+\;B(x)\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)=\log p_{\theta^{*}}(x)\;+\;B(x)\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(x)=f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(x)=f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is (to first order) a nondecreasing function of the scalar <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Replacing <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> in both numerator and denominator incurs only
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})</annotation></semantics></math> relative error, so</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[\,w\,B\,]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[\,w\,]}+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[\,w\,B\,]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[\,w\,]}+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]=\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]=\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)</annotation></semantics></math> because
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[B]=\varepsilon^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[u_{\theta^{*}}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[B]=\varepsilon^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[u_{\theta^{*}}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are nondecreasing (as functions of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>), the monotone-covariance inequality yields
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, with strict <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> unless <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a.e. constant or <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is degenerate.
Therefore <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> to first order, i.e.
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>
(up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]</annotation></semantics></math> implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi=\frac{\langle\varepsilon,F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}=-\,\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\;\leq\;0\quad(\text{strict }&lt;0\text{ generically})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>strict </mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> generically</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi=\frac{\langle\varepsilon,F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}=-\,\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\big\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\;\leq\;0\quad(\text{strict }&lt;0\text{ generically}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Consequence.</em> Combining Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6 (Mode-seeking ⇒ cos𝜑&lt;0 (first order)). ‣ Common AR samplers are mode-seeking. ‣ B.4 Acute-angle conditions that imply 𝑠&lt;0 (AR models) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> with Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem B.4 (Directional upper bound for 𝑠). ‣ Angle and magnitudes. ‣ B.3 An upper bound on 𝑠 and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for sufficiently small <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> (and the explicit window follows by substituting <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}=F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}=F</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Acute-angle conditions that imply <math id="A2.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (diffusion &amp; flow)</h3>

<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Loss and geometry.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use standard pathwise quadratic losses. For diffusion score models,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{diff}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\Big[\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s_{\theta}(X_{t},t)-s^{\star}(X_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\;dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>diff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{diff}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\Big[\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s_{\theta}(X_{t},t)-s^{\star}(X_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\;dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and for flow matching,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{flow}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\Big[\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|v_{\theta}(X_{t},t)-v^{\star}(X_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\;dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>flow</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{flow}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\Big[\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|v_{\theta}(X_{t},t)-v^{\star}(X_{t},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\;dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\theta,t}(x):=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}^{(t)}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\theta,t}(x):=\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}^{(t)}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{t}(x):=\partial_{\theta}\phi_{\theta,t}(x)\!\big|_{\theta^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{t}(x):=\partial_{\theta}\phi_{\theta,t}(x)\!\big|_{\theta^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the pathwise Fisher</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{path}}:=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\big[J_{t}(X_{t})J_{t}(X_{t})^{\top}\big]\;dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{path}}:=\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}}\!\big[J_{t}(X_{t})J_{t}(X_{t})^{\top}\big]\;dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the angle (mirroring the AR case)</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi_{\text{path}}\;:=\;\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\;F_{\text{path}}^{-1}b_{\text{path}}\big\rangle_{F_{\text{path}}}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F_{\text{path}}}\,\big\|F_{\text{path}}^{-1}b_{\text{path}}\big\|_{F_{\text{path}}}},\qquad b_{\text{path}}:=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\Big[\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\,\phi_{\theta^{*},t}(X_{t})\,dt\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi_{\text{path}}\;:=\;\frac{\big\langle\varepsilon,\;F_{\text{path}}^{-1}b_{\text{path}}\big\rangle_{F_{\text{path}}}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F_{\text{path}}}\,\big\|F_{\text{path}}^{-1}b_{\text{path}}\big\|_{F_{\text{path}}}},\qquad b_{\text{path}}:=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\Big[\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\,\phi_{\theta^{*},t}(X_{t})\,dt\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Anti-alignment corresponds to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi_{\text{path}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi_{\text{path}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Finite-step ODE solvers are mode-seeking.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the probability-flow ODE with velocity
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>; for diffusion,
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
An explicit one-step scheme with step size <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k-1}=x_{k}+h\,f(x_{k},t_{k}),\qquad J_{k}:=\frac{\partial x_{k-1}}{\partial x_{k}}=I+h\,\nabla_{x}f(x_{k},t_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k-1}=x_{k}+h\,f(x_{k},t_{k}),\qquad J_{k}:=\frac{\partial x_{k-1}}{\partial x_{k}}=I+h\,\nabla_{x}f(x_{k},t_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}\log(I+A)=\mathrm{tr}(A)-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}(A^{2})+O(\|A\|^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}\log(I+A)=\mathrm{tr}(A)-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}(A^{2})+O(\|A\|^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=h\,\nabla_{x}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=h\,\nabla_{x}f</annotation></semantics></math>
(and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(A^{2})=\|A\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(A^{2})=\|A\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{x}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{x}f</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric; otherwise take its symmetric part),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}f)\;-\;\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\;+\;O(h^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}f)\;-\;\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\;+\;O(h^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Chaining steps and comparing to the exact ODE yields a terminal reweight of the reference law:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x_{0})\ \propto\ \exp\!\Big\{\tfrac{h}{2}\,\bar{C}(x_{0})+o(h)\Big\}\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0}),\qquad\bar{C}(x_{0}):=\frac{1}{T}\,\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}f(X_{t_{k}},t_{k})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\,\Big|\,X_{0}=x_{0}\Big],\ \ T\asymp 1/h." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x_{0})\ \propto\ \exp\!\Big\{\tfrac{h}{2}\,\bar{C}(x_{0})+o(h)\Big\}\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0}),\qquad\bar{C}(x_{0}):=\frac{1}{T}\,\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}f(X_{t_{k}},t_{k})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\,\Big|\,X_{0}=x_{0}\Big],\ \ T\asymp 1/h.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For diffusion, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{x}f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}^{2}\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{x}f(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,\nabla_{x}^{2}\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}(x_{0})=\frac{1}{T}\,\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\sigma(t_{k})^{4}\,\|\nabla_{x}^{2}\log p_{t_{k}}(X_{t_{k}})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\,\Big|\,X_{0}=x_{0}\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}(x_{0})=\frac{1}{T}\,\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\sigma(t_{k})^{4}\,\|\nabla_{x}^{2}\log p_{t_{k}}(X_{t_{k}})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\,\Big|\,X_{0}=x_{0}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptionx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptionx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption</span></span><span id="Thmassumptionx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(A-MONO: curvature–density coupling)<span id="Thmassumptionx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptionx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\mapsto\bar{C}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\mapsto\bar{C}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is weakly increasing in <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e.,
if <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})\leq\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})\leq\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}(x_{0})\leq\bar{C}(x_{0}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}(x_{0})\leq\bar{C}(x_{0}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuition. Finite-step integrators overweight trajectories with stronger contraction
(large <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{x}f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{x}f\|</annotation></semantics></math>). Near modes, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is more curved, contraction is larger,
hence <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> grows with local density. As <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>, the bias vanishes and
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\!\to\!p_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\!\to\!p_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> (neutral).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Step-size scaling)<span id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}f)-\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}f)-\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the per-step excess contraction is <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing over <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\asymp 1/h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\asymp 1/h</annotation></semantics></math> steps yields the terminal reweight exponent
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h}{2}\,\bar{C}(x_{0})+o(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h}{2}\,\bar{C}(x_{0})+o(h)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the pathwise linear bias
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\text{path}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\,\phi_{\theta^{*},t}(X_{t})\,dt]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\text{path}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\int_{0}^{1}\omega(t)\,\phi_{\theta^{*},t}(X_{t})\,dt]</annotation></semantics></math> obeys
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b_{\text{path}}\|_{F_{\text{path}}^{-1}}=O(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b_{\text{path}}\|_{F_{\text{path}}^{-1}}=O(h)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the curvature tilt
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{\text{path}}\|_{\mathrm{op},F_{\text{path}}^{-1}}=O(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>path</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mtext>path</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{\text{path}}\|_{\mathrm{op},F_{\text{path}}^{-1}}=O(h)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Both vanish linearly as <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, making the sampler neutral in the limit.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Flow matching.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For updates <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k-1}=x_{k}+h\,v_{\theta}(x_{k},t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k-1}=x_{k}+h\,v_{\theta}(x_{k},t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}v_{\theta})\;-\;\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{tr}\!\big((\nabla_{x}v_{\theta})^{2}\big)+O(h^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\det J_{k}=h\,\mathrm{tr}(\nabla_{x}v_{\theta})\;-\;\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{tr}\!\big((\nabla_{x}v_{\theta})^{2}\big)+O(h^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}v_{\theta}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}=\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\|\nabla_{x}v_{\theta}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}+O(h^{3})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and the same reweight <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
With the flow analogue of A-MONO (the conditional expectation of
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}v_{\theta}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}v_{\theta}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> increasing in <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>),
finite-step flow solvers are likewise mode-seeking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Classifier-free guidance (CFG) is mode-seeking.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CFG modifies the diffusion velocity via a guided score</p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\gamma}(x,t)\;=\;s_{\text{uncond}}(x,t)\;+\;\gamma\big(s_{\text{cond}}(x,t)-s_{\text{uncond}}(x,t)\big),\qquad\gamma&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\gamma}(x,t)\;=\;s_{\text{uncond}}(x,t)\;+\;\gamma\big(s_{\text{cond}}(x,t)-s_{\text{uncond}}(x,t)\big),\qquad\gamma&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so the probability-flow velocity becomes <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,s_{\gamma}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}(x,t)=-\sigma(t)^{2}\,s_{\gamma}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Repeating the derivation above with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\!\to\!f_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\!\to\!f_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the same reweight form</p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\gamma}(x_{0})\ \propto\ \exp\!\Big\{\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\,C_{\gamma}(x_{0})+o(h^{2})\Big\}\,p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}(x_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\gamma}(x_{0})\ \propto\ \exp\!\Big\{\tfrac{h^{2}}{2}\,C_{\gamma}(x_{0})+o(h^{2})\Big\}\,p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}(x_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <em id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">guided</em> reference law and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\gamma}(x_{0})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}(X_{t_{k}},t_{k})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\ \Big|\ X_{0}=x_{0}\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\gamma}(x_{0})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\Big[\sum_{k}\|\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}(X_{t_{k}},t_{k})\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\ \Big|\ X_{0}=x_{0}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}=-\sigma^{2}\big(\nabla_{x}s_{\text{uncond}}+\gamma\,\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}=-\sigma^{2}\big(\nabla_{x}s_{\text{uncond}}+\gamma\,\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}=\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\;+\;2\gamma\,\big\langle\nabla_{x}f,\;-\sigma^{2}\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big\rangle_{\mathrm{Fr}}\;+\;\gamma^{2}\,\big\|\!-\,\sigma^{2}\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>Fr</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{x}f_{\gamma}\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}=\|\nabla_{x}f\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}\;+\;2\gamma\,\big\langle\nabla_{x}f,\;-\sigma^{2}\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big\rangle_{\mathrm{Fr}}\;+\;\gamma^{2}\,\big\|\!-\,\sigma^{2}\nabla_{x}(s_{\text{cond}}-s_{\text{uncond}})\big\|_{\mathrm{Fr}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Near condition-relevant modes, the guidance term increases the magnitude (and contraction) of the flow,
so <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\gamma}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\gamma}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is larger in higher-density regions of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{r},\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>; this is the same
curvature–density coupling as A-MONO, now for the guided dynamics.
Hence finite-step CFG is mode-seeking in the sense above, and becomes neutral as <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Neighbor models: stability and uniform Neon improvement</h3>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix the synthetic sampler <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> generated once at the reference
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">frozen</em>). Consider any
<em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">neighbor</em> checkpoint</p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}\;=\;\theta_{r}+\delta\;=\;\theta^{*}+(\varepsilon+\delta),\qquad\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}\ \text{small}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>small</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}\;=\;\theta_{r}+\delta\;=\;\theta^{*}+(\varepsilon+\delta),\qquad\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}\ \text{small}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All quantities below (gradients, alignments) are evaluated at <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, but the
synthetic law remains <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Local expansions at a neighbor.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the same first-order argument as in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Neon improves under anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{n}:=\varepsilon+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{n}:=\varepsilon+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{d}(\theta_{n})\;=\;H_{d}\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon_{n}\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),\qquad r_{s}(\theta_{n})\;=\;H_{d}\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;b\;+\;\Delta\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon_{n}\|_{H_{d}}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{d}(\theta_{n})\;=\;H_{d}\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon_{n}\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),\qquad r_{s}(\theta_{n})\;=\;H_{d}\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;b\;+\;\Delta\,\varepsilon_{n}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon_{n}\|_{H_{d}}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\kappa}=b+\Delta\,\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\kappa}=b+\Delta\,\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\phi_{\theta^{*}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\phi_{\theta^{*}}]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta:=\mathbb{E}_{q}[J_{\theta^{*}}]-\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[J_{\theta^{*}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta:=\mathbb{E}_{q}[J_{\theta^{*}}]-\mathbb{E}_{p_{\text{data}}}[J_{\theta^{*}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
(as in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 An upper bound on 𝑠 and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>). Define <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta):=\langle r_{d}(\theta),P\,r_{s}(\theta)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta):=\langle r_{d}(\theta),P\,r_{s}(\theta)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Alignment is locally Lipschitz in a neighborhood)<span id="Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mI\preceq K\preceq MI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mI\preceq K\preceq MI</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}:=\|b\|_{H_{d}^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}:=\|b\|_{H_{d}^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}:=\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op},\,H_{d}^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}:=\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op},\,H_{d}^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exist constants <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (depending only on <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,\eta_{0},\eta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,\eta_{0},\eta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the local
regularity from (A2)) such that, for all sufficiently small <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\,s(\theta_{n})-s(\theta_{r})\,\big|\;\leq\;C_{1}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+\eta_{0}+1\big)\,\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}\;+\;C_{2}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+1\big)\,\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}^{\,2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\,s(\theta_{n})-s(\theta_{r})\,\big|\;\leq\;C_{1}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+\eta_{0}+1\big)\,\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}\;+\;C_{2}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+1\big)\,\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}^{\,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous at <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and varies at most linearly
with <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> to first order.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Insert equation <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Local expansions at a neighbor. ‣ B.6 Neighbor models: stability and uniform Neon improvement ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> into <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta)=\langle r_{d},Pr_{s}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)=\langle r_{d},Pr_{s}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and whiten with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d:=H_{d}^{1/2}\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d:=H_{d}^{1/2}\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> to write (cf. Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 An upper bound on 𝑠 and sufficient conditions for anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>)</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta)\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and likewise with <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\to a+d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\to a+d</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(a+d)-s(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(a+d)-s(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and bounding each term with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|K\|_{\mathrm{op}}=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|K\|_{\mathrm{op}}=M</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{\Delta}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\eta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{\Delta}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\eta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}=\eta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}=\eta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
yields the stated linear-plus-quadratic control in <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|d\|_{2}=\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|d\|_{2}=\|\delta\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform anti-alignment in a ball)<span id="Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta_{r})\leq-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta_{r})\leq-\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for some margin <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\;&gt;\;0\quad\text{such that}\quad C_{1}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+\eta_{0}+1\big)\,\rho\;+\;C_{2}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+1\big)\,\rho^{2}\;\leq\;\tfrac{\mu}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">such that</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\;&gt;\;0\quad\text{such that}\quad C_{1}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+\eta_{0}+1\big)\,\rho\;+\;C_{2}\big(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}+1\big)\,\rho^{2}\;\leq\;\tfrac{\mu}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s(\theta)\leq-\mu/2&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)\leq-\mu/2&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every neighbor <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta-\theta_{r}\|_{H_{d}}\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta-\theta_{r}\|_{H_{d}}\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uniform Neon improvement for a set of neighbors.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}\subseteq\{\theta:\|\theta-\theta_{r}\|_{H_{d}}\leq\rho\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}\subseteq\{\theta:\|\theta-\theta_{r}\|_{H_{d}}\leq\rho\}</annotation></semantics></math> be any finite
collection of neighbor checkpoints. Perform one short synthetic fine-tune at each
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (same frozen <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>) to obtain
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}(\theta)=\theta-\alpha Pr_{s}(\theta)+O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}(\theta)=\theta-\alpha Pr_{s}(\theta)+O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the Neon
merge <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{Neon}}(\theta)=(1+w)\theta-w\,\theta_{s}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Neon</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{Neon}}(\theta)=(1+w)\theta-w\,\theta_{s}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Single <math id="Thmtheorem10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> that safely improves all neighbors)<span id="Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., by Cor. <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Corollary B.9 (Uniform anti-alignment in a ball). ‣ Local expansions at a neighbor. ‣ B.6 Neighbor models: stability and uniform Neon improvement ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>).
Assume either (i) <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{d}(\theta):=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{d}(\theta):=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,
or (ii) a uniform directional curvature bound holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\theta)^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\!\big(\theta+\tau d(\theta)\big)\,d(\theta)\;\leq\;L_{\mathrm{dir}}\,\|d(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\quad\text{for all }\theta\in\mathcal{N},\ \tau\in[0,\tau_{0}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\theta)^{\top}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\!\big(\theta+\tau d(\theta)\big)\,d(\theta)\;\leq\;L_{\mathrm{dir}}\,\|d(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\quad\text{for all }\theta\in\mathcal{N},\ \tau\in[0,\tau_{0}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\theta):=Pr_{s}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\theta):=Pr_{s}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{\min}:=\min_{\theta\in\mathcal{N}}s(\theta)\;&lt;\;0,\qquad Q_{\max}:=\max_{\theta\in\mathcal{N}}r_{s}(\theta)^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}(\theta)\,P\,r_{s}(\theta)\ \ \text{(or }L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\text{ under (ii))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(or </mtext><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> under (ii))</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\min}:=\min_{\theta\in\mathcal{N}}s(\theta)\;&lt;\;0,\qquad Q_{\max}:=\max_{\theta\in\mathcal{N}}r_{s}(\theta)^{\top}P^{\top}\widehat{H}_{d}(\theta)\,P\,r_{s}(\theta)\ \ \text{(or }L_{\mathrm{dir}}\|d(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\text{ under (ii))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then any</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;&lt;\;w\;&lt;\;-\,\frac{2\,s_{\min}}{\alpha\,Q_{\max}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;&lt;\;w\;&lt;\;-\,\frac{2\,s_{\min}}{\alpha\,Q_{\max}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">guarantees
<math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\!\big(\theta_{\text{Neon}}(\theta)\big)\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Neon</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}\!\big(\theta_{\text{Neon}}(\theta)\big)\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> (up to <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O((w\alpha)^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O((w\alpha)^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>)
<em id="Thmtheorem10.p1.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">for every</em> <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply the one-step expansion from Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem B.1 (One-step Neon improvement). ‣ Alignment scalar and synthetic objective. ‣ B.2 Neon improves under anti-alignment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> at each <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
and take the worst-case (most conservative) quadratic coefficient and the most negative linear term.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Practical takeaway)<span id="Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If a single base checkpoint <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits anti-alignment with margin
(negative <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>), then <em id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> sufficiently close neighbors inherit
<math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus benefit from the same Neon recipe. In practice, one can
either (a) choose a single conservative <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> that safely improves an entire
validation-selected pool of nearby models, or (b) tune <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> per checkpoint using
its local <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and curvature proxy.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Cross-architecture transfer)<span id="Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The same frozen sampler <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> can safely improve a <em id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">nearby</em> checkpoint from a <em id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">different</em> architecture, provided the two models are close in the data-risk geometry.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Concretely, let models <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{B})</annotation></semantics></math> share the same per-example loss <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and data, with
<math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}:=\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> their (population) Hessians at the same minimizer <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Generate <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> once at a reference <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})}</annotation></semantics></math> for model <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider a neighbor <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})}</annotation></semantics></math> for model <math id="Thmtheorem12.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{B})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If the Hessians are <em id="Thmtheorem12.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">spectrally close</em> and their norms are equivalent on the relevant subspace, i.e. there exist <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c\leq C&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c\leq C&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and a small <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\,\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\leq\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}}\leq C\,\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\quad\text{and}\quad\big\|H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}-H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\big\|_{\mathrm{op},\,\left(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\right)^{-1}}\leq\zeta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\,\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\leq\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}}\leq C\,\|v\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\quad\text{and}\quad\big\|H_{d}^{(\mathsf{B})}-H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\big\|_{\mathrm{op},\,\left(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\right)^{-1}}\leq\zeta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and the sampler-induced terms are close,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b^{(\mathsf{B})}-b^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})})^{-1}}+\|\Delta^{(\mathsf{B})}-\Delta^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{\mathrm{op},\,\left(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\right)^{-1}}\;\leq\;\zeta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>op</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b^{(\mathsf{B})}-b^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})})^{-1}}+\|\Delta^{(\mathsf{B})}-\Delta^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{\mathrm{op},\,\left(H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}\right)^{-1}}\;\leq\;\zeta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p3.3" class="ltx_p">then the alignment scalar <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> transfers continuously:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\,s^{(\mathsf{B})}(\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})})-s^{(\mathsf{A})}(\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})})\,\big|\;\leq\;\underbrace{O(\zeta)}_{\text{cross-arch mismatch}}\;+\;\underbrace{O\!\big(\|\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})}-\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\big)}_{\text{neighbor shift}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>cross-arch mismatch</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>neighbor shift</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\,s^{(\mathsf{B})}(\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})})-s^{(\mathsf{A})}(\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})})\,\big|\;\leq\;\underbrace{O(\zeta)}_{\text{cross-arch mismatch}}\;+\;\underbrace{O\!\big(\|\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})}-\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})}\|_{H_{d}^{(\mathsf{A})}}\big)}_{\text{neighbor shift}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Hence, if <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(\mathsf{A})}(\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})})\leq-\mu&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(\mathsf{A})}(\theta_{r}^{(\mathsf{A})})\leq-\mu&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with margin and the cross-architecture mismatch <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and neighbor distance are small enough, then <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(\mathsf{B})}(\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(\mathsf{B})}(\theta_{n}^{(\mathsf{B})})</annotation></semantics></math> remains negative. In turn, Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem B.10 (Single 𝑤 that safely improves all neighbors). ‣ Uniform Neon improvement for a set of neighbors. ‣ B.6 Neighbor models: stability and uniform Neon improvement ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a> provides a single merge weight <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> that (to second order) reduces <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously for the <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{B})</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors. Practically, using a <em id="Thmtheorem12.p3.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">common</em> preconditioner <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> defined in a data-geometry (e.g., an empirical <math id="Thmtheorem12.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate) further stabilizes cross-architecture transfer.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>When self-training helps</h3>

<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">First-order effect of self-training.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A short synthetic fine-tune takes the step <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}+O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding first-order change in real-data risk is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{s})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;=\;-\,\alpha\,\underbrace{\langle r_{d},\;Pr_{s}\rangle}_{s}\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})\;=\;-\,\alpha\,s\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>s</mi></munder></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{s})-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta_{r})\;=\;-\,\alpha\,\underbrace{\langle r_{d},\;Pr_{s}\rangle}_{s}\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})\;=\;-\,\alpha\,s\;+\;O(\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self-training helps</em> (decreases <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>) when <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Directional <em id="Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">lower</em> bound for <math id="Thmtheorem13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> small,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\geq\;(m-M\,\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;M\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\geq\;(m-M\,\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;M\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">All <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are in <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the local expansions,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}PH_{d}\varepsilon\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}Pb\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}P\Delta\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}PH_{d}\varepsilon\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}Pb\;-\;\varepsilon^{\top}H_{d}P\Delta\varepsilon\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Whiten with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:=H_{d}^{1/2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}b</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}:=H_{d}^{-1/2}\Delta H_{d}^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=H_{d}^{1/2}PH_{d}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}\,a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;=\;a^{\top}Ka\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;-\;a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}\,a\;+\;O(\|a\|_{2}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Lower bound each term:
(i) <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}Ka\geq m\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}=m\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}Ka\geq m\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}=m\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii) Write <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}K\tilde{b}=\|K^{1/2}a\|\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|\cos\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}K\tilde{b}=\|K^{1/2}a\|\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|\cos\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> the Euclidean angle between <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{1/2}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1/2}a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{1/2}\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1/2}\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;\geq\;-\,\|K^{1/2}a\|\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|\,[{-}\cos\theta]_{+}\;\geq\;-\,M\,\|a\|_{2}\,\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\;\geq\;-\,\|K^{1/2}a\|\,\|K^{1/2}\tilde{b}\|\,[{-}\cos\theta]_{+}\;\geq\;-\,M\,\|a\|_{2}\,\|\tilde{b}\|_{2}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we used <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|K^{1/2}x\|\leq\sqrt{M}\|x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|K^{1/2}x\|\leq\sqrt{M}\|x\|</annotation></semantics></math> and identify <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> (the <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>–angle between <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}^{-1}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}^{-1}b</annotation></semantics></math>) with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> up to whitening. This gives
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\geq-\,M\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,[{-}\cos\varphi]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-a^{\top}K\tilde{b}\geq-\,M\,\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,[{-}\cos\varphi]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(iii) <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\geq-\,\|K\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|\tilde{\Delta}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|a\|_{2}^{2}\geq-\,M\,\eta_{1}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\,a^{\top}K\tilde{\Delta}a\geq-\,\|K\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|\tilde{\Delta}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|a\|_{2}^{2}\geq-\,M\,\eta_{1}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combine (i)–(iii) and absorb <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|a\|_{2}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Natural-gradient geometry)<span id="Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=H_{d}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=H_{d}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=I</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m{=}M{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m{=}M{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>) and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\geq\;(1-\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\geq\;(1-\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;-\;\eta_{0}\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}\,\big[{-}\cos\varphi\big]_{+}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diversity-seeking samplers make <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> positive (locally).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We say <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">diversity-seeking</em> if <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x)\propto f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x)\propto f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))\,p_{\theta_{r}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">nonincreasing</em> and not a.e. constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Diversity-seeking <math id="Thmtheorem15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (first order))<span id="Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the NLL specialization (<math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\theta}=-u_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\theta}=-u_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}=F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}=F</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]</annotation></semantics></math>), if <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing then, for <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}=\theta^{*}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\;\geq\;0\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\;\geq\;0\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x):=\varepsilon^{\top}u_{\theta^{*}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x):=\varepsilon^{\top}u_{\theta^{*}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. As in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Acute-angle conditions that imply 𝑠&lt;0 (AR models) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)=\log p_{\theta^{*}}(x)+B(x)+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x)=\log p_{\theta^{*}}(x)+B(x)+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(x)=f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(x)=f(\log p_{\theta_{r}}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is (to first order) a <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">nonincreasing</em> function of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Replacing <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> in
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[wB]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[w]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[wB]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta_{r}}}[w]}</annotation></semantics></math>
incurs only <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})</annotation></semantics></math> relative error, hence
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[w]}+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[w]}+O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Monotone covariance with <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">opposite</em> monotonicities gives
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}(w,B)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>; since <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[B]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[B]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta^{*}}}[wB]\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> to first order. Therefore
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\varepsilon,\;F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\rangle_{F}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\leq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\varepsilon,\;F^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]\rangle_{F}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[B]\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math>
and with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=-\mathbb{E}_{q}[u_{\theta^{*}}]</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi=\frac{\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi=\frac{\langle\varepsilon,\,F^{-1}b\rangle_{F}}{\|\varepsilon\|_{F}\|F^{-1}b\|_{F}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>
up to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\varepsilon\|_{F})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Self-training helps near good models under diversity seeking)<span id="Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing (diversity seeking) so that Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma B.15 (Diversity-seeking ⇒ cos𝜑≥0 (first order)). ‣ Diversity-seeking samplers make 𝑠 positive (locally). ‣ B.7 When self-training helps ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.15</span></a> gives <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> to first order. Then, for sufficiently small <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}&lt;m/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}&lt;m/M</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;\geq\;(m-M\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})\;&gt;\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;\geq\;(m-M\eta_{1})\,\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}\;+\;O(\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{3})\;&gt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the self-training step <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}\!\mapsto\!\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}\!\mapsto\!\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-\alpha Pr_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">decreases</em> <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> to first order. In the natural-gradient case (<math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=H_{d}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=H_{d}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>), it suffices that <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lower bound in Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem B.13 (Directional lower bound for 𝑠). ‣ First-order effect of self-training. ‣ B.7 When self-training helps ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a> is a “quadratic minus linear” form:
the curvature-controlled term <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-M\eta_{1})\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-M\eta_{1})\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> pushes <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive</em>, while the bias term subtracts only when <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Diversity-seeking samplers have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma B.15 (Diversity-seeking ⇒ cos𝜑≥0 (first order)). ‣ Diversity-seeking samplers make 𝑠 positive (locally). ‣ B.7 When self-training helps ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.15</span></a>), so their <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">leading</em> behavior is <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\!\gtrsim\!(m-M\eta_{1})\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≳</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\!\gtrsim\!(m-M\eta_{1})\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, close to a good model (small <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon\|_{H_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and with modest curvature tilt (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> small), <em id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self-training helps</em> whereas Neon’s reversal would not.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Examples.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:.5cm;">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">High temperature in AR</span> (<math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\propto p_{\theta_{r}}^{1/\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\propto p_{\theta_{r}}^{1/\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>  ( <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z)=e^{(1/\tau-1)z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=e^{(1/\tau-1)z}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing ) <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> diversity-seeking, <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\varphi\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\varphi\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> to first order.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Anti-mode truncations</span>: procedures that downweight peaks and upweight tails (e.g., sampling after complementary filtering of top-<math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> mass) are nonincreasing transforms of <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>; the same conclusion applies.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.8 </span>Notes on finite synthetic set and effect of short fine-tuning</h3>

<div id="A2.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main analysis assumes an infinite synthetic pool and uses the population synthetic gradient.
In practice, we generate one fixed synthetic set <math id="A2.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and perform a brief fine-tune before Neon.
This subsection formalizes the effect of <em id="A2.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">finite</em> <math id="A2.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <em id="A2.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">short</em> fine-tuning on the direction used by Neon and on its dependence on <math id="A2.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a synthetic dataset <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn once from <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> and then kept fixed. Let <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x,\zeta;\theta)\in\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x,\zeta;\theta)\in\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be the per-example gradient of the synthetic loss (with internal randomness <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., diffusion time/noise), and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}(x;\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}\!\big[g(x,\zeta;\theta)\big],\qquad r_{s}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\bar{g}(x;\theta)\big],\qquad r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bar{g}(x_{i};\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}(x;\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{\zeta}\!\big[g(x,\zeta;\theta)\big],\qquad r_{s}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big[\bar{g}(x;\theta)\big],\qquad r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bar{g}(x_{i};\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Short fine-tuning (FT) from <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> uses step size <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps, and a positive-definite preconditioner <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{k+1}=\theta_{k}-\alpha\,P\,\widehat{r}_{k},\qquad\widehat{r}_{k}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g\big(x_{i},\zeta_{i,k};\theta_{k}\big),\quad k=0,\dots,T-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k+1}=\theta_{k}-\alpha\,P\,\widehat{r}_{k},\qquad\widehat{r}_{k}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g\big(x_{i},\zeta_{i,k};\theta_{k}\big),\quad k=0,\dots,T-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\zeta_{i,k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\zeta_{i,k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are fresh draws each time the fixed examples are reused. Let <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}:=\theta_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}:=\theta_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the scaled displacement</p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}:=\frac{\theta_{s}-\theta_{r}}{\alpha T}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}:=\frac{\theta_{s}-\theta_{r}}{\alpha T}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two finite-sample errors.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Dataset error (finite <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>):</em> at <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\big[r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big]=r_{s}(\theta_{r}),\qquad\mathrm{Cov}\!\big(r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big)=\frac{1}{n}\,\Sigma_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.622em;" width="1.622em"><mi>Cov</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\big[r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big]=r_{s}(\theta_{r}),\qquad\mathrm{Cov}\!\big(r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big)=\frac{1}{n}\,\Sigma_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\mathrm{data}}:=\mathrm{Cov}_{x\sim q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big(\bar{g}(x;\theta_{r})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\mathrm{data}}:=\mathrm{Cov}_{x\sim q_{\theta_{r},\kappa}}\!\big(\bar{g}(x;\theta_{r})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> and irreducible unless <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Monte Carlo (MC) error in time/noise:</em> write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}_{k}=r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{k})+\xi_{k},\qquad\mathbb{E}[\xi_{k}\mid\theta_{k}]=0,\quad\mathrm{Cov}(\xi_{k}\mid\theta_{k})=\Sigma_{\mathrm{mc}}(\theta_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>mc</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}_{k}=r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{k})+\xi_{k},\qquad\mathbb{E}[\xi_{k}\mid\theta_{k}]=0,\quad\mathrm{Cov}(\xi_{k}\mid\theta_{k})=\Sigma_{\mathrm{mc}}(\theta_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Local smoothness.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{s}(\theta):=\nabla_{\theta}r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{s}(\theta):=\nabla_{\theta}r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume there exists <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{dir}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{dir}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r}+\tau v)-r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})-\tau\,H_{s}(\theta_{r})v\,\right\|_{2}\ \leq\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,L_{\mathrm{dir}}\,\tau^{2}\,\|v\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r}+\tau v)-r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})-\tau\,H_{s}(\theta_{r})v\,\right\|_{2}\ \leq\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,L_{\mathrm{dir}}\,\tau^{2}\,\|v\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Short-FT displacement)<span id="Thmtheorem17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under equation <a href="#A2.E7" title="In Setup. ‣ B.8 Notes on finite synthetic set and effect of short fine-tuning ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a> and equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="In Local smoothness. ‣ B.8 Notes on finite synthetic set and effect of short fine-tuning ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, if <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T\leq c/L_{\mathrm{dir}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T\leq c/L_{\mathrm{dir}}</annotation></semantics></math> for a small absolute constant <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}=-\,P\!\left(\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\xi_{k}\,\right)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\!\Big(\alpha T\,\|PH_{s}(\theta_{r})\|_{\mathrm{op}}\ \|r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.611em;" width="0.611em"><mi>P</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.654em;" width="0.654em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}=-\,P\!\left(\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\xi_{k}\,\right)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\!\Big(\alpha T\,\|PH_{s}(\theta_{r})\|_{\mathrm{op}}\ \|r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Direction concentration)<span id="Thmtheorem18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}\!\big(\Sigma_{\mathrm{mc}}(\theta)\big)\leq\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>mc</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}\!\big(\Sigma_{\mathrm{mc}}(\theta)\big)\leq\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in a neighborhood of <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any unit vector <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\langle u,\ d_{T}+P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\right\rangle^{2}\right]\ \leq\ \frac{\|P\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\sigma^{2}}{T}\ +\ C^{2}\,(\alpha T)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\langle u,\ d_{T}+P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\right\rangle^{2}\right]\ \leq\ \frac{\|P\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\sigma^{2}}{T}\ +\ C^{2}\,(\alpha T)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{dir}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{dir}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|PH_{s}(\theta_{r})\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|PH_{s}(\theta_{r})\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}\ \xrightarrow{\ \mathbb{P}\ }\ -\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.778em">→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℙ</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}\ \xrightarrow{\ \mathbb{P}\ }\ -\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning-rate note (why “small” helps).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem17" title="Lemma B.17 (Short-FT displacement). ‣ Local smoothness. ‣ B.8 Notes on finite synthetic set and effect of short fine-tuning ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem18" title="Proposition B.18 (Direction concentration). ‣ Local smoothness. ‣ B.8 Notes on finite synthetic set and effect of short fine-tuning ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a> show the curvature bias of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> scales like <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\alpha T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\alpha T)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the MC variance shrinks like <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/T</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus decreasing <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> reduces bias (keeps the trajectory in the local linear region) but does not change the <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/T</annotation></semantics></math> variance term; increasing <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> averages MC noise but increases bias unless <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is reduced so that <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T</annotation></semantics></math> stays small. A practical regime is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T\ \leq\ \frac{c}{L_{\mathrm{dir}}}\quad\text{and}\quad T\ \text{large enough that}\ \frac{\|P\|_{\mathrm{op}}\sigma}{\sqrt{T}}\ \ll\ \|P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>large enough that</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≪</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T\ \leq\ \frac{c}{L_{\mathrm{dir}}}\quad\text{and}\quad T\ \text{large enough that}\ \frac{\|P\|_{\mathrm{op}}\sigma}{\sqrt{T}}\ \ll\ \|P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quadratic proxy for Neon and finite <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{d}(\theta_{r}):=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{d}(\theta_{r}):=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}:=\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}:=\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{data}}(\theta)\big|_{\theta_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathcal{S}}:=\big\langle r_{d}(\theta_{r}),\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big\rangle,\qquad z_{\mathcal{S}}:=\big(r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big)^{\top}P^{\top}H_{d}\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathcal{S}}:=\big\langle r_{d}(\theta_{r}),\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big\rangle,\qquad z_{\mathcal{S}}:=\big(r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})\big)^{\top}P^{\top}H_{d}\,P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the Neon merge <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{Neon}}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>Neon</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{Neon}}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and short FT, the real-risk change admits the local expansion</p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{R}(w)\ \approx\ w\alpha\,s_{\mathcal{S}}\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,(w\alpha)^{2}\,z_{\mathcal{S}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{R}(w)\ \approx\ w\alpha\,s_{\mathcal{S}}\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,(w\alpha)^{2}\,z_{\mathcal{S}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with minimizer and minimum</p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}=-\frac{s_{\mathcal{S}}}{\alpha z_{\mathcal{S}}},\qquad\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\ \approx\ -\,\frac{s_{\mathcal{S}}^{2}}{2\,z_{\mathcal{S}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}=-\frac{s_{\mathcal{S}}}{\alpha z_{\mathcal{S}}},\qquad\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\ \approx\ -\,\frac{s_{\mathcal{S}}^{2}}{2\,z_{\mathcal{S}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as a plug-in estimate for <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{s}_{T}:=\langle r_{d}(\theta_{r}),-d_{T}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}_{T}:=\langle r_{d}(\theta_{r}),-d_{T}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{z}_{T}:=\langle d_{T},H_{d}d_{T}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{z}_{T}:=\langle d_{T},H_{d}d_{T}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{s}_{T}=s_{\mathcal{S}}+\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\big(T^{-1/2}+\alpha T\big),\qquad\widehat{z}_{T}=z_{\mathcal{S}}+\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\big(T^{-1/2}+\alpha T\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{s}_{T}=s_{\mathcal{S}}+\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\big(T^{-1/2}+\alpha T\big),\qquad\widehat{z}_{T}=z_{\mathcal{S}}+\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\big(T^{-1/2}+\alpha T\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{w}^{\*}\approx-\widehat{s}_{T}/(\alpha\widehat{z}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{w}^{\*}\approx-\widehat{s}_{T}/(\alpha\widehat{z}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates on <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!\to\!\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!\to\!\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Why performance vs. <math id="Thmtheorem19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> is U-shaped)<span id="Thmtheorem19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}=r_{s}+\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}=r_{s}+\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}}(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathcal{S}}=\langle r_{d},Pr_{s}\rangle+\langle r_{d},P\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\rangle,\qquad z_{\mathcal{S}}=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}H_{d}Pr_{s}\;+\;\text{(cross/}\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\text{ terms)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mtext>(cross/</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> terms)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathcal{S}}=\langle r_{d},Pr_{s}\rangle+\langle r_{d},P\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\rangle,\qquad z_{\mathcal{S}}=r_{s}^{\top}P^{\top}H_{d}Pr_{s}\;+\;\text{(cross/}\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\text{ terms)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For very small <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>, variance dominates: <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> are noisy and the attainable improvement <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\!\approx\!-s_{\mathcal{S}}^{2}/(2z_{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msubsup><mpadded style="width:0.608em;" width="0.608em"><mo>≈</mo></mpadded><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\!\approx\!-s_{\mathcal{S}}^{2}/(2z_{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> is weak. For very large <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>, variance vanishes (<math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathcal{S}}\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>) but the synthetic direction <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Pr_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Pr_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> tends to align with high-curvature eigenvectors of <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by mode-seeking samplers, increasing <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> faster than <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{\mathcal{S}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{\mathcal{S}}|</annotation></semantics></math> grows; consequently <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\,\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\,|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\,\Delta\mathcal{R}^{\*}_{\mathcal{S}}\,|</annotation></semantics></math> shrinks slightly. A moderate <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> balances these effects: variance is small enough to stabilize <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> while the direction has not collapsed onto the sharpest curvature, keeping <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> moderate. This yields the empirically observed U-shaped curve in Neon performance as a function of <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Takeaway.</span> With a fixed, finite synthetic set generated once, <em id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">short</em> fine-tuning (small <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, modest <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha T</annotation></semantics></math> is small) produces a variance-reduced and reliable estimate of the synthetic gradient direction <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\,r_{s}^{(\mathcal{S})}(\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>, stabilizing the empirical coefficients <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{\mathcal{S}},z_{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{\mathcal{S}},z_{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the merge weight <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. Very small <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> is variance-limited; very large <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> inflates <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> via curvature, so a broad, <em id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">moderate</em> <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> is typically best.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.9 </span>Toy Experiment</h3>

<div id="A2.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we present a toy experiment to empirically validate and provide deeper intuition for the theoretical results presented in the paper. The goal is to create a controlled environment where we can directly observe the effects of sampler behavior on self-training and measure the key theoretical quantity: the directional alignment between gradients.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task is to learn a 2D Gaussian distribution, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\text{ref}},\Sigma_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\text{ref}},\Sigma_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where the mean is <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{ref}}=[0,0]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{ref}}=[0,0]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and the covariance is <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{ref}}=[2,1;1,2]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{ref}}=[2,1;1,2]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use a small Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Model (DDPM) with an MLP backbone, trained over a short diffusion process of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=20</annotation></semantics></math> steps with a cosine noise schedule. A base model, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, is trained for a long duration (<math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs) on a small dataset of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{base}}=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{base}}=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> real samples with a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure it has converged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To control the sampler’s behavior during synthetic data generation, we introduce a scalar hyperparameter, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, which directly scales the model’s score. The standard score is defined as <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)=-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t)/\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)=-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t)/\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the model’s noise prediction. During sampling, we use a modified score, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{\theta}(x_{t},t)=\zeta\cdot s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{\theta}(x_{t},t)=\zeta\cdot s_{\theta}(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math>, to generate samples. This allows us to precisely control the sampler’s characteristics:</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:.5cm;">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>: The sampler becomes <em id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mode-seeking</em>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>: The sampler becomes <em id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">diversity-seeking</em>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=1</annotation></semantics></math>: The sampler is neutral.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment 1: FID vs. Merge Weight.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our first experiment, we validate the main prediction of our paper. We generate synthetic datasets using a mode-seeking sampler (<math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=1.1</annotation></semantics></math>) and a diversity-seeking sampler (<math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>). We then fine-tune <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> on each of these datasets to obtain a self-trained model <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. We form a merged model via the one-parameter extrapolation formula:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{w}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-w(\theta_{s}-\theta_{r})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{w}=(1+w)\theta_{r}-w\theta_{s}=\theta_{r}-w(\theta_{s}-\theta_{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A positive weight (<math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) corresponds to Neon’s <em id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">negative extrapolation</em>, moving away from the self-trained model. A negative weight (<math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) corresponds to <em id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive extrapolation</em> (interpolation). Letting <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the formula becomes <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{w}=(1-\alpha)\theta_{r}+\alpha\theta_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{w}=(1-\alpha)\theta_{r}+\alpha\theta_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is standard interpolation and equivalent to a step of self-training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results, shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F1" title="Figure B.1 ‣ Experiment 1: FID vs. Merge Weight. ‣ B.9 Toy Experiment ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Detailed Explanations ‣ Neon: Negative Extrapolation From Self-Training Improves Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, perfectly match our theory. For the mode-seeking sampler, the optimal FID is achieved at <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstrating that negative extrapolation (Neon) helps. Conversely, for the diversity-seeking sampler, the optimal FID is achieved at <math id="A2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{*}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{*}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, showing that positive extrapolation (self-training) is beneficial.</p>
</div>
